Add ReferenceAndSample records as braced aggregates.

ReferenceAndSample is an aggregate; vector::emplace_back(ref, value) constructs it through C++20's
parenthesized aggregate initialization (P0960), which Chromium's clang 16 predates (see 0001).
push_back({ref, value}) builds the same record with the same members.

--- a/base/metrics/persistent_histogram_allocator.cc
+++ b/base/metrics/persistent_histogram_allocator.cc
@@ -220,3 +220,3 @@
     if (found_id == match_id) {
-      found_records.emplace_back(ref, value);
+      found_records.push_back({ref, value});
       found = true;
@@ -226,3 +226,3 @@
       CHECK(samples);
-      samples->emplace_back(ref, value);
+      samples->push_back({ref, value});
     }
